.TH DFEEDTEST 8
.SH NAME
dfeedtest \- show which dnewsfeeds labels and spool an article would go to
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dfeedtest
[
.B \-a
]
[
.B \-n
.I newsgroups
]
[
.B \-D
.I distribution
]
[
.B \-s
.I size
]
[
.B \-p
.I numpath
]
[
.B \-t
.I arttype
]
[
.B \-M
.I message-id
]
[
.B \-h
]
[
.B \-S
]
[
.B \-l
.I label
]
[
.B \-N
.I dnewsfeeds
]
[
.B \-F
]
[
.B \-X
]
[
.BR \-d [\fIn\fP]
]
[
.B \-C
.I diablo.config
]
[
.B \-V
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I dfeedtest
loads dnewsfeeds (and, with
.BR \-X ,
dspool.ctl) the way diablo does and shows where an article with the given
properties would go.  It is a way to check a feed or spool change before
diablo reloads it; it doesn't talk to a running server.
.PP
The article is described with options, or read from standard input with
.BR \-a .
A newsgroups list is required.  The program prints the article properties
it used, then one line
.BI "Matched: " label
for every label that would be fed the article.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-a
Read an article (headers and body) from standard input and take the
Newsgroups, Distribution, Message-ID, number of Path entries, size and
article type from it.
.TP
.BI \-n " newsgroups"
The Newsgroups header, a comma-separated list.
.TP
.BI \-D " distribution"
The Distribution header (default: none).
.TP
.BI \-s " size"
The article size in bytes (default 1000).
.TP
.BI \-p " numpath"
The number of Path entries (default 1).
.TP
.BI \-t " arttype"
The article type, for example binary or mime (default: plain text).
.TP
.BI \-M " message-id"
The Message-ID.
.TP
.B \-h
Match as a header-only article.
.TP
.B \-S
Match as spam.
.TP
.BI \-l " label"
Load only this dnewsfeeds label.  With \fB\-F\fP, dump only this label.
.TP
.BI \-N " dnewsfeeds"
Use this dnewsfeeds file instead of the one in diablo.config.
.TP
.B \-F
Print diablo's in-memory view of dnewsfeeds (all labels, or the one given
with \fB\-l\fP) and exit.
.TP
.B \-X
Print the spool the article would be stored in instead of the matching
labels: a spool number, or NoSpool, RejectArt or DontStore.
.TP
.BR \-d [\fIn\fP]
Set the debug level and trace the dnewsfeeds matching.
.TP
.BI \-C " diablo.config"
Use this diablo.config instead of the default.
.TP
.B \-V
Print the version and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
dfeedtest -n comp.lang.c,misc.test -s 5000
dfeedtest -a < article
dfeedtest -n alt.binaries.test -t binary -X
dfeedtest -F -l reader
.fi
